      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Adding to this, when building the animation curves in C#, if I feed the the value '1e-45' in for the animation curve, for allow grabbing as True. (3e-45 for Other, 0 for false)\n\nEg; in my script\n\n`SetCurve(gameObjectToAnimate, typeof(VRCPhysBoneBase), \"allowGrabbing\", 1e-45)`\n\nthe animation value '1.4011e-45' is still shown in the animation value - but the Editor appears to respect it.\n\nI'll be taking this animation into game shortly and checking the results.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
